                "entry_id": "cca357f6-c9fa-36a7-85df-079c47d882e9",
                "word": "labialization",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "0a164624-5e13-43be-b1b6-a1664b939033",
                        "entry_id": "cca357f6-c9fa-36a7-85df-079c47d882e9",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "labializations"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "67f22ec1-1667-36f0-9a4f-a05a98187cf8",
                        "entry_id": "cca357f6-c9fa-36a7-85df-079c47d882e9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A secondary articulatory feature of usually consonants that involves the contraction or rounding of the lips (labia) during pronunciation."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a1254123-0d94-49fb-87a5-a3239991fe5d",
                                "sense_id": "67f22ec1-1667-36f0-9a4f-a05a98187cf8",
                                "text": "These labialized stops are of course nothing but positionally determined allophones of the [t] and the [k] phoneme, and their labialization is non-distinctive"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d1839714-8cb0-46c8-a425-f98bbf6ac0e1",
                                "sense_id": "67f22ec1-1667-36f0-9a4f-a05a98187cf8",
                                "text": "The second question concerns the reasons for the labialization of this suffix in [1.3] - in the case of artukluk one immediately thinks of an assimilation (*u - ı > u - u)"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "80099dce-f94f-42b9-8b30-10f21896d0a3",
                        "source_entry_id": "cca357f6-c9fa-36a7-85df-079c47d882e9",
                        "source_sense_id": "67f22ec1-1667-36f0-9a4f-a05a98187cf8",
                        "source_sense_description": "secondary articulatory feature",
                        "target_lang_word": "labialisation",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "labialisation",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c07ddc79-0d12-339a-96dc-78f0979cf1d1",
                                        "entry_id": "be12aa66-5400-3e60-b184-fcf98ef57699",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Action de labialiser, utilisation des lèvres comme dispositif secondaire d’articulation, pendant que le reste de la bouche produit un autre phonème."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Phonétique"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "492ac738-d33c-4379-b5f9-fd70008362c1",
                                                "sense_id": "c07ddc79-0d12-339a-96dc-78f0979cf1d1",
                                                "text": "Bien que la labialisation ne soit en aucune façon universelle parmi les langues du monde, elle est cependant extrêmement répandue."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1df9aa66-2030-4284-96e7-100f76e22c62",
                                                "sense_id": "c07ddc79-0d12-339a-96dc-78f0979cf1d1",
                                                "text": "En effet, le traducteur peut être influencé par la labialisation du correspondant direct en français d’un signe en particulier."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ae90fe42-b899-47cf-bfe8-4006b0b3bb32",
                        "source_entry_id": "cca357f6-c9fa-36a7-85df-079c47d882e9",
                        "source_sense_id": "67f22ec1-1667-36f0-9a4f-a05a98187cf8",
